    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Mary is correct: $6!=720$ ways.\n\nTreat AA and GG as separate blocks. Their identical letters were never permuted internally, so no further factorial division is needed.",
      "worked": "With the A’s together and the G’s together, the six distinct elements are AA, GG, L, R, N and E.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=6!\\\\N&=720\\end{align*}$$\n\nMary’s count is correct for these blocks. Bob’s further division is unnecessary because neither the A’s nor the G’s were permuted within their blocks.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
